  "id": "COMPOUND:17212 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between Ethyl 2-acetamido-2-(dimethylamino)acetate and SF-188, mediated through the target SNU-387. This compound appears to act as a common intermediary, with multiple pathways linking it to SF-188 through different molecular targets. SNU-387 is identified as a target of two distinct compounds: (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside. Both of these compounds are linked to SF-188 via their respective targets, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving SNU-387 as a central node in the pathway. The evidence supports a possible role for Ethyl 2-acetamido-2-(dimethylamino)acetate in modulating SNU-387 activity, which in turn influences SF-188. The consistent presence of SNU-387 as a common target across different compounds strengthens the hypothesis that this molecule is a key mediator in the interaction between the drug and SF-188.",
